{
    desc => 'Regex n navigates across empty lines',
    description => <<'END_DESC',
Action: /m. then n repeatedly — must skip empty lines correctly

Regression test for GTK forward_to_line_end bug on empty lines.
Bug: line_text() returned next-line content for empty lines,
causing search_forward to find matches beyond the empty line's
actual length. set_cursor clamped the out-of-bounds column to 0,
creating an infinite loop where n kept "finding" the same match.

_1.png (initial state):
- Dark theme, Normal mode, cursor at line 0, col 0
- Multiple empty lines between content

Action: keystrokes "/m.\\n" (search regex m., press Enter)

_2.png (search + first n):
- Search highlights visible on all m. matches (mi, me, me, me, mo, mo, mo, ma, mo, me, ma, me)
- Cursor on first match: "mi" in "Vim" (line 0, col 4)
- First n moves to "me" in "Documentation" (line 0, col 19)

Action: keystrokes "n" (second n)

_3.png (second n — crosses empty line):
- n skips past "me" in Documentation, crosses the empty line (line 1),
  lands on "me" in "Version" (line 2, col 14)
- Search highlights still visible on all matches

Action: keystrokes "nnn" (three more n presses)

_4.png (after three more n):
- Cursor advances through Normal(mo), Motions(mo), move(mo)
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->editor->set_theme('dark');
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(200);
        $ctx->snapshot('1');
        $ctx->delay(200);
        $ctx->keys('/m.\n');
        $ctx->delay(500);
        $ctx->keys('n');
        $ctx->delay(300);
        $ctx->snapshot('2');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('n');
        $ctx->delay(300);
        $ctx->snapshot('3');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('nnn');
        $ctx->delay(300);
        $ctx->snapshot('4');
    },
}
